<title>CANADA: Northern Telecom says buys software firm.</title>
<headline>Northern Telecom says buys software firm.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northern Telecom Ltd said on Thursday it agreed to buy the assets of Pasadena, California-based AGL Systems Inc for an undisclosed sum.</p>
<p>Nortel said AGL specializes in the development of intelligent, real-time application software for the telecommunications industry.</p>
<p>The company will be a unit of Nortel's Broadband Carrier Networks Group.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100</p>
